  "worked_solution": "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=0.$ Substituting $y(1)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(1)=3.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032} & =9{c}_{1}{t}^{8}+{c}_{2}{t}^{8}+9{c}_{2}{t}^{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{\u2032}(1)=3$ and ${c}_{1}=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =9{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 3 & =0+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
